# Register layer rules

Consult [agent/DATASHEET.md](agent/DATASHEET.md) for figure references.

## Validate-at-setup / trust-at-encode

- `validate_config()` at configure time — width, range, enum, profile gates
- `encode_register()` masks widths; does not re-check ranges on hot path

## Register file

- Staleness = diff of encoded `_current` vs `_last_written` (no dirty flags)
- `configure()` is transactional: rollback on validation failure
- Figure 23 DBR: R1/R2 changes force trailing R0 write
- Figure 23 DBB: R4 divider change forces R0 when R2 `double_buffer` set
- DBB state read from encoded R2 word, not a separate flag

## Commit API

- `commit_plan()` — minimal stale set; use for retunes
- `commit_all_plan()` — all six registers; use at power-up / divider boundaries
- Both return words only (R5→R0) — no cache update until `mark_written()`
- `WORKED_WORDS[i]` = register Ri; SPI order is reversed for a full write

## Profile gates

ADF4350 vs ADF4351 differences enforced in validation, not bypassed in encode.
See [agent/DATASHEET.md](agent/DATASHEET.md) feature matrix.

## device.py

Only module that imports `machine`. SPI: LE low → 4-byte write → LE high → low.
